1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,433
<i> Thank you.</i>

2
00:00:01,567 --> 00:00:03,400
<i>Because of you, Father is free.</i>

3
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:04,233
<i> We won.</i>

4
00:00:04,367 --> 00:00:05,133
<i> Why are you following me?</i>

5
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:05,867
<i> I'm going with you.</i>

6
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,700
<i> You've given up on Joey.</i>

7
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:08,733
<i> She likes someone else.</i>

8
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:09,600
<i> Did she say that?</i>

9
00:00:09,733 --> 00:00:11,433
<i> If I go after what I want,</i>

10
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:13,900
<i>I will not stop
until she's mine.</i>

11
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:15,067
<i> Why are you still there?</i>

12
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,800
<i>If you don't want
to force me to kick you out,</i>

13
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:17,600
<i> leave now!</i>

14
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:18,833
<i> Don't worry about it.</i>

15
00:00:18,967 --> 00:00:20,967
<i>Be thankful he's just asking you
to hide.</i>

16
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,433
<i> I want my revenge.</i>

17
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:25,133
<i>I'll even take a video of her
while I kill her.</i>

18
00:00:25,267 --> 00:00:26,933
<i> Call it poetic justice.</i>

19
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:29,667
<i>I'm a little hesitant
about Jin Ho</i>

20
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,233
<i> searching for Theresa Park</i>

21
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,833
<i>because he doesn't want
to cooperate with the police.</i>

22
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,267
<i>There's nothing wrong with that.</i>

23
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,367
<i> Get out of the car.</i>

24
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,267
<i> Get out!</i>

25
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,833
<i> I'm so happy you caught me.</i>

26
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:40,900
<i>I'm in trouble.
I need you, Baby.</i>

27
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:43,000
<i>I was going to talk to you two.</i>

28
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:44,633
<i> I'm going home to my place.</i>

29
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:46,367
<i> I want to be with my family.</i>

30
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:48,767
<i>Of course, you've been dreaming
about it for a long time.</i>

31
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,400
<i>If you need anything, just call.</i>

32
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:52,900
<i> See you around, Boss Budol.</i>

33
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:54,500
<i> See you, JoeyOnDuty.</i>

34
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:55,867
<i> You left me.</i>

35
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,833
<i>Let's finish what we started
together.</i>

36
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:00,500
<i>You should take care those kinds
of friends.</i>

37
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:04,933
<i>I hope we can be together again
without any trouble.</i>

38
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:07,333
<i>Now that we're not worried
about Theresa,</i>

39
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,100
<i>let's focus on the real problem.</i>

40
00:01:09,233 --> 00:01:11,433
<i>He can't make us look weak,
Matias.</i>

41
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:13,200
<i>I'll take care of that, Berdugo.</i>

42
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:38,633
Our school starts next week.

43
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:42,000
Besides, even though I'm already
in studying in Manila,

44
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:44,767
I'll still come here
every weekend.

45
00:01:45,733 --> 00:01:46,800
Oh my,

46
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,433
you know,

47
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:52,433
my plan,

48
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:55,500
is to say goodbye
to Ma'am Yvette.

49
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,567
now that your father
is back home.

50
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,767
Aren't you going to volunteer
anymore, Mother?

51
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:04,900
You know, Clarissa, if you're
happy with that foundation,

52
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:07,033
why are you quitting?

53
00:02:07,167 --> 00:02:09,633
I'll take care of the house
first.

54
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,300
- Really?
- Yes, of course!

55
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:15,867
You know...

56
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:19,667
You know, I'm really happy
with my job.

57
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,667
It's a great feeling
when you help people.

58
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,167
See.

59
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,400
And you, Father,
what's your plan?

60
00:02:27,533 --> 00:02:29,567
Are you going to be
a househusband?

61
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,633
Are you not going back
to the service?

62
00:02:33,367 --> 00:02:37,167
You know, Joey, all I know
how to do is police work.

63
00:02:39,167 --> 00:02:43,033
But if I go back to the service,
I'll let you know.

64
00:02:43,167 --> 00:02:44,600
Really?

65
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:45,567
Is that true?

66
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:46,867
Yes.

67
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,900
Joey, we'll just believe him
if he's going to pull this

68
00:02:53,067 --> 00:02:55,433
and the tower doesn't fall.

69
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:57,633
That's the only time we'll
believe him.

70
00:02:57,767 --> 00:02:58,333
Really?

71
00:02:58,467 --> 00:02:59,900
Okay.

72
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:01,500
This, this, this.

73
00:03:01,633 --> 00:03:03,400
If it doesn't collapse.

74
00:03:04,967 --> 00:03:06,767
- I told you!
- No!

75
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:08,667
I told you you're not going
to be left behind here.

76
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,000
It slipped!

77
00:03:10,133 --> 00:03:14,067
- You know your father.
- Promise, it just slipped!

78
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,633
Hey!

79
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:23,167
I don't know if I should
congratulate you

80
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:26,800
because I know what you've been
through was not easy.

81
00:03:26,933 --> 00:03:30,767
But I'm happy that you've
overcome all that.

82
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,200
Your acquittal is final.

83
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:35,400
You're also out of trouble
with internal affairs.

84
00:03:35,533 --> 00:03:38,300
You're really free now,
Major Delgado.

85
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:40,200
Thank you very much, Chief.

86
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:43,867
About your re instatement...

87
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,300
I took the liberty of sending
a recommendation.

88
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:51,367
All that's missing
is a formal request from you.

89
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,400
I'll take care of the approval.

90
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:56,600
Chief, if I could,

91
00:03:56,767 --> 00:03:59,367
I'd give my family
some time first.

92
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:07,433
Miguel, you are one of the good
ones in the force.

93
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:09,233
There are only a few of you.

94
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:11,833
Besides, I know you.

95
00:04:11,967 --> 00:04:16,000
You wouldn't be at peace if you
didn't catch the syndicate

96
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:17,567
that's going after you.

97
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:22,267
But Mother's calmer now,

98
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,400
since the last time
I visited her, right?

99
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,467
I noticed that too.

100
00:04:27,633 --> 00:04:31,133
You know, it's been a while
since she softened up like that.

101
00:04:31,267 --> 00:04:33,500
That's it. I hope it continues.

102
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:35,867
Including her giving attention
to me.

103
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,200
You know, she just needs time.

104
00:04:38,333 --> 00:04:42,733
Anyway, who are you interviewing
in Bolagos?

105
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:44,533
It's Major Miguel Delgado,
Yvette.

106
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:46,700
Are you interviewing
Miguel Delgado?

107
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:48,933
Yeah.

108
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:53,333
Isn't your show focused on
exposés?

109
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,467
And let's be honest, Andrew.

110
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:00,067
Your show is a bit anti-police.

111
00:05:01,433 --> 00:05:05,133
Yes, and that's exactly
what I want to change, Tomas.

112
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:07,967
I'm not actually anti-police.

113
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,167
I'm anti-lies, anti-crime,
and anti-corruption.

114
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:16,367
Because I believe there
are still good police officers,

115
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,033
and Major Miguel Delgado
is one of them.

116
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:26,033
It's funny that you sound
very impressed with him,

117
00:05:26,167 --> 00:05:29,833
knowing that you don't know him
that well.

118
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,433
Fair point, Hon,

119
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:39,400
but we shouldn't be judging too
quickly.

120
00:05:39,533 --> 00:05:43,467
Remember, that's why we wanted
to help Clarissa back then.

121
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:47,867
I know, I just don't want Andrew
walking in blind.

122
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:53,567
It's hard to trust
someone you don't really know.

123
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,900
Well, I've talked to him
a couple of times

124
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:58,033
during the investigation, Tomas,

125
00:05:58,167 --> 00:06:01,700
and I think I know enough
to know that he's a good one.

126
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:06,267
So what exactly do you know?

127
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:10,900
Hold on. Excuse me.

128
00:06:15,967 --> 00:06:17,533
Yes, Peter? You called.

129
00:06:17,667 --> 00:06:19,300
I am worried about Jin Ho.

130
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:20,433
He still hasn't come home

131
00:06:20,567 --> 00:06:24,067
since he said he'd keep
an eye on Theresa.

132
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,500
That was just the other day.

133
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:29,033
Wait. No text or call, nothing?

134
00:06:29,167 --> 00:06:31,933
Nothing, Bro. Cannot be reached.

135
00:06:32,067 --> 00:06:38,367
Okay, maybe he caught Theresa
and took her to South Korea.

136
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,533
Wow, Seriously?

137
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:43,300
What? He didn't even say
goodbye, just like that?

138
00:06:43,433 --> 00:06:47,133
Well, Peter,
we barely know this guy.

139
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:48,733
<i> What if he's really like that?</i>

140
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:51,433
After a mission, it's over,
he goes home.

141
00:06:51,567 --> 00:06:52,767
No attachments.

142
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,000
Andrew knows a lot about
Delgado.

143
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,167
And the way he talks about him,

144
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,500
it's obvious that he's on
his side.

145
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,867
I tried to keep him out
of this mess,

146
00:07:10,067 --> 00:07:11,600
but this is what he wants.

147
00:07:11,733 --> 00:07:14,833
Your brother-in-law is really
a liability, Berdugo.

148
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,900
He'll give Delgado a scene.

149
00:07:18,033 --> 00:07:19,800
<i> He wants to make him a hero.</i>

150
00:07:19,933 --> 00:07:22,267
Well, okay,
let's give it to him.

151
00:07:23,833 --> 00:07:24,533
Major!

152
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:26,500
Andrew! How are you?

153
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:29,567
I'm sorry, it's a bit difficult
to come here to Bolagos,

154
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:30,867
and then I'm late.

155
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,200
It's okay, Major,
it's just a few minutes.

156
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:35,633
I'm sorry.

157
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,633
Joey, is she there?

158
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:41,867
She's not here.
She's at home with his mother.

159
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,100
Do you need anything from her?

160
00:07:44,233 --> 00:07:47,300
Andrew, what do you need?

161
00:07:50,733 --> 00:07:53,300
- Let's go set up, Kyle.
- That's what I said.

162
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,133
It's about Jin Ho.

163
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:04,867
Peter told me he hasn't been
home since the surveillance.

164
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,267
Jin Ho?

165
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:09,267
I know he's South Korean
intelligence, right?

166
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:12,000
Don't worry,

167
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:13,833
I'll talk to my colleagues
at the precinct.

168
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:17,000
I'll see if they have any
information about this guy.

169
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:18,500
Okay.

170
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:19,833
Let's go, Major.

171
00:08:23,367 --> 00:08:26,067
When the camera is pointed
at Delgado,

172
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,600
he stops being a reporter.

173
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:31,500
<i>He becomes his weapon
to bring us down.</i>

174
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,767
And I can't afford a weapon
being pointed at us,

175
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:38,500
even if he is family.

176
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,700
I guess some things
really never stay solid.

177
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:45,000
What now, Berdugo?

178
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:48,167
Should I include him with
what I'm cooking for Delgado?

179
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,067
Not really,

180
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:53,833
but I want you to send him
and Delgado a warning.

181
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
<i>Make it loud and make it
personal.</i>

182
00:08:57,133 --> 00:08:58,367
Copy, Berdugo.

183
00:08:59,933 --> 00:09:03,533
I released the exposé
to the public, Major,

184
00:09:03,667 --> 00:09:05,600
and I have to own up to that.

185
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:08,700
I'm responsible for that,
not because I want to,

186
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:13,433
but because that's my job,
to lay out information.

187
00:09:14,633 --> 00:09:19,200
But it's also my duty
to fix my mistake,

188
00:09:19,333 --> 00:09:23,700
especially when life
and reputation depend on it.

189
00:09:25,833 --> 00:09:27,967
Major, I just want to ask.

190
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:31,433
When everything was against you,

191
00:09:31,567 --> 00:09:35,133
what do you hold onto to keep
you from giving up?

192
00:09:35,267 --> 00:09:37,133
Of course, it's the truth.

193
00:09:38,233 --> 00:09:40,933
<i> I know it's not my fault.</i>

194
00:09:41,067 --> 00:09:43,467
<i>I don't care what
other people say.</i>

195
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:50,633
But the worst part of it was
that my own family doubted me.

196
00:09:52,367 --> 00:09:54,267
When they lost trust in me,

197
00:09:57,367 --> 00:10:00,333
that was probably the worst pain
I've ever felt,

198
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:03,067
and how can I regain that trust?

199
00:10:04,367 --> 00:10:06,667
I'm doing all this for them.

200
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:10,700
<i> I'm fighting for them.</i>

201
00:10:10,833 --> 00:10:13,767
I'm also grateful to the others

202
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,233
who I never thought
would help me.

203
00:10:16,367 --> 00:10:18,800
But the fight isn't over yet,
Major.

204
00:10:18,933 --> 00:10:20,600
The ones in the video,

205
00:10:20,733 --> 00:10:25,300
alias Theresa Park and alias
Loloy are still at large.

206
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:31,867
And of course, the head of
the syndicate that set you up,

207
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,933
and also at large.

208
00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:34,767
You know, you're right.

209
00:10:34,933 --> 00:10:36,467
Like as they say,

210
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,000
"We're just getting
to the exciting part."

211
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:43,167
As long as those syndicates
are there,

212
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,833
those drugs won't run out.

213
00:10:45,967 --> 00:10:49,033
And that will ruin a lot
of young lives.

214
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:52,867
So we must destroy them.

215
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,667
Let's finish them off.

216
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:00,633
Matias.

217
00:11:01,833 --> 00:11:03,467
It's ready, Berdugo.

218
00:11:10,633 --> 00:11:14,767
The syndicate will definitely
come back for you, Major.

219
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:18,500
This Major's life is dangerous.

220
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:26,033
For sure, there's a bounty on
his head as if he had no family.

221
00:11:26,167 --> 00:11:28,167
They might get into trouble
with you.

222
00:11:29,433 --> 00:11:35,467
Major, have you thought of a way
to expose those syndicates?

223
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,833
You know, Andrew...

224
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:44,433
What happened?

225
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,900
What's that?

226
00:11:50,033 --> 00:11:52,000
What happened?
Why did it disappear?

227
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:54,367
Our live was cut.

228
00:12:17,567 --> 00:12:18,633
Hey!

229
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,267
He blew our tire.

230
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,733
Crazy! Who is that?

231
00:12:28,867 --> 00:12:31,133
Who else knows about this
interview?

232
00:12:31,267 --> 00:12:32,433
A lot, Major.

233
00:12:32,567 --> 00:12:35,867
We advertised your interview
so that many people can watch.

234
00:12:41,633 --> 00:12:42,833
Call him.

235
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,233
Hello, Joey?

236
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:53,300
Hello, Father?

237
00:12:53,433 --> 00:12:54,400
Miguel?

238
00:12:54,533 --> 00:12:55,800
How are you?

239
00:12:55,933 --> 00:12:56,967
We're fine.

240
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,467
Are you sure?

241
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,000
And Andrew?

242
00:13:00,133 --> 00:13:01,233
He's okay...

243
00:13:01,367 --> 00:13:03,200
No one was hurt. We're fine.

244
00:13:03,333 --> 00:13:04,600
Miguel, go home!

245
00:13:04,733 --> 00:13:07,000
Go home, quick!

246
00:13:07,133 --> 00:13:08,233
Okay, okay, I'm on my way home.

247
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:09,733
Be careful, Father.

248
00:13:10,967 --> 00:13:12,567
What happened?

249
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,867
My God.

250
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:20,067
I think they're targeting me.

251
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,000
Target?

252
00:13:21,167 --> 00:13:22,933
But why did they target the bus?

253
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:24,567
Why didn't he come
after you inside?

254
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:29,467
Maybe a warning so I don't talk.

255
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,867
Oh my, maybe we're being
warned too, Andrew.

256
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,367
We've covered for Major Delgado
a few times already.

257
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,300
Maybe we seemed like we're on
his allies.

258
00:13:40,567 --> 00:13:42,300
What's that?

259
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:43,700
Wait, what are we going to do,
Boss?

260
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:45,100
I still love my life.

261
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:47,467
Let's be careful.

262
00:13:48,633 --> 00:13:51,133
But that doesn't mean
we're going to give up

263
00:13:51,267 --> 00:13:52,733
just because we were
intimidated.

264
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,633
They can't win.

265
00:13:57,767 --> 00:14:00,967
Evil will prevail even more
when no one fights back,

266
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,100
so we won't give up.

267
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,200
Hello, Yvette?

268
00:14:20,433 --> 00:14:22,767
Yeah, we're good, I'm good.

269
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,333
No one got hurt, thankfully.
Okay.

270
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,233
Father...

271
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,333
Thank God you're safe.

272
00:14:31,467 --> 00:14:32,467
Father, how are you?

273
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:34,733
Did you find out
who did that to you?

274
00:14:35,967 --> 00:14:38,033
You've only been out
for a few days,

275
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:39,800
and something like this
is happening?

276
00:14:46,567 --> 00:14:48,800
There's something I wanted
to tell you.

277
00:14:51,733 --> 00:14:54,033
I know you don't want trouble,

278
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,567
but I can't abandon my duty
as a police officer.

279
00:15:00,367 --> 00:15:02,500
As long as those syndicates
are around,

280
00:15:03,967 --> 00:15:06,267
they'll ruin many lives.

281
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,633
Andrew is right.

282
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:14,833
Evil prevails when no one
fights back.

283
00:15:17,733 --> 00:15:19,767
So I'm going back
to the service.

284
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:22,767
I'm going to finish this fight.

285
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:32,600
If it were me, Miguel,
I wouldn't allow you.

286
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:38,000
I don't want to repeat the
hardship we went through before.

287
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:44,267
But I love you,

288
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:46,967
and I know that if I stop you,

289
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:49,467
you'll regret it for the rest
of your life

290
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,000
that you didn't do anything.

291
00:15:52,933 --> 00:15:55,733
So whatever your decision is,

292
00:15:55,867 --> 00:15:57,333
I'm on your side.

293
00:15:59,467 --> 00:16:00,567
Thank you.

294
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:04,600
Clarissa,

295
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:06,633
after this mission is over,

296
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,933
I'll retire.

297
00:16:11,533 --> 00:16:12,833
That's a promise.

298
00:16:15,467 --> 00:16:17,567
We're just here for you, Father.

299
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:20,400
Never say die?

300
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,267
Never say die.

301
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:38,233
This is an important day not
only for the Bolagos Police

302
00:16:38,367 --> 00:16:40,833
but for the entire police force.

303
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:47,300
Today, we are reinstating one
of our brave police officers.

304
00:16:47,433 --> 00:16:51,533
By the authority vested in me
as Bolagos chief of police

305
00:16:51,667 --> 00:16:54,233
and upon the directive
of the Regional command,

306
00:16:56,433 --> 00:16:59,267
I hereby reinstate you
to service,

307
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:01,233
Major Miguel Delgado.

308
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:09,633
Welcome back, Major Delgado.

309
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:12,333
Reporting for duty, Sir!

310
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,033
I can see Delgado.

311
00:18:00,367 --> 00:18:01,233
Sorry.

312
00:18:03,433 --> 00:18:04,533
Wait a minute.

313
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,133
Do you know Major?

314
00:18:06,267 --> 00:18:07,933
Just passing by, Sir.

315
00:18:08,067 --> 00:18:09,933
I looked, and there were a lot
of people.

316
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:11,067
Okay, Sir.

317
00:18:14,333 --> 00:18:16,433
The day isn't over yet.

318
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:18,033
I'll finish you later.

319
00:18:26,067 --> 00:18:27,633
What else do you need?

320
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,600
Just a moment, Mother.

321
00:18:38,733 --> 00:18:39,800
Okay.

322
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:09,667
Andrew, you might choke.

323
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:15,767
Thank you.

324
00:19:22,033 --> 00:19:25,533
I'm rushing to preview
the footage

325
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:27,933
so I can send it to my editor.

326
00:19:33,267 --> 00:19:34,367
Thank goodness,

327
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,867
none of your belongings
were damaged on the bus

328
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,833
when you and Father
were attacked.

329
00:19:39,967 --> 00:19:41,533
Actually,

330
00:19:41,667 --> 00:19:43,667
two tires were damaged,

331
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,200
but I got them fixed

332
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:48,867
so we can go back to Manila.

333
00:19:50,967 --> 00:19:53,133
It's a good thing we met today.

334
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,133
Did you miss me?

335
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:00,700
Of course!

336
00:20:07,667 --> 00:20:10,333
I mean, of course,
I miss that we're complete,

337
00:20:10,467 --> 00:20:12,767
with Jin Ho and Peter.

338
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,267
You know,
you're really assuming!

339
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:18,033
Am I really the one assuming?
You said you missed me.

340
00:20:18,167 --> 00:20:19,233
No, no!

341
00:20:19,367 --> 00:20:20,833
What I mean is when we were
together.

342
00:20:20,967 --> 00:20:23,233
I'll go ahead,
I've been bothering you.

343
00:20:40,533 --> 00:20:42,800
This is the coordination letter
you requested.

344
00:20:42,933 --> 00:20:45,300
Whatever you heard,
it can't get out.

345
00:20:45,433 --> 00:20:47,333
What's up with the town
of Balmora?

346
00:20:47,467 --> 00:20:49,133
The deal is already sealed.

347
00:20:49,267 --> 00:20:50,867
He still wants to see me
in person.

348
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,833
But once we meet,
the deal is sealed.

349
00:20:53,967 --> 00:20:54,767
Hey!

350
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:55,533
It's me!

351
00:20:55,667 --> 00:20:56,800
Big brother!

352
00:20:56,933 --> 00:20:57,767
Peter!

353
00:20:59,033 --> 00:21:00,633
I missed you! It's been a while!

354
00:21:00,767 --> 00:21:02,300
I'm going to give you something.

355
00:21:02,433 --> 00:21:04,867
So you won't forget Mother
and me.

356
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,367
We've already prepared
everything we need for him.

357
00:21:08,633 --> 00:21:10,167
It's his first day
in the service,

358
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,800
and his last day in the world.

359
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:14,067
The thorn in our throats
is gone.

360
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,233
Have you seen this?

361
00:21:15,367 --> 00:21:16,700
Do not contact me again.

362
00:21:16,833 --> 00:21:19,400
- Joey's father is dead, Jin Ho.
- What?
